00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.429 align:start position:0%
 
did you know they're making a new  resident evil we haven't seen this  beloved storied horror franchise since  well anyway they're making a new one the  eighth mainline game in the series in  fact  simply titled resident evil village  thanks to capcom's recent showcase we  now have a  pretty good idea of what the game is  from what it's about  to how it plays to when it's coming out  spoilers  it's really soon this video is going to  tell you everything you need to know  about resident evil village  and maybe you'll learn why everyone is  super thirsty for that very tall vampire  lady  if you find this video useful we'd  really appreciate a like and sub  but hey the fact that you're here  already means a lot  now let's talk resident evil  village is a follow-up to 2017's  resident evil 7  biohazard and you are once again set in  the shoes of ethan winters village takes  place a few years after the events of  the baker mansion  and ethan and his wife mia have settled  down after all that  madness and getting busy apparently  because they have a  child now a daughter in fact side note  resident evil 7 has two endings one  where mia dies  and one where she lives the mia lives  ending has become the canonical ending  that village goes off of  the plot kicks off when ethan's home is  invaded his daughter  kidnapped and mia seemingly murdered  ethan's quest to save his daughter leads  him to the titular  village but who took his daughter and  why  well it's looking like series poster boy  chris redfield is responsible  why chris has long been the series  lawful good  boy scout sure he's had his low points  but he always rises to the occasion to  do what's right and  punch his way through large boulders and  into our hearts  which makes the horrible actions he's  committed against ethan's family  all the more shocking why chris has gone  off the deep end like this will no doubt  be one of the game's  biggest mysteries the box art of the  game shows the brooding face of redfield  mirrored with a  werewolf does chris turn into a werewolf  cause  that would be incredible it's entirely  possible that this  isn't even the real chris redfield after  all he's looking a lot  beefier than the last time we saw him  but also  that chris is slimmer than the one  punching the boulder  but that chris is different from the one  in code veronica which to be perfectly  frank looks  nothing like this guy and you know what  chris's true role as a villain or hero  is still left up for debate but we still  have a very clear-cut villain in lady  demotrescu  well ethan winters you escaped  my little brother's idiot games did you  she is the owner of a  massive castle that looms over the  village the common people are  terrified of the place and demitrescu  and as we've seen from the recently  released  maiden demo those who enter the castle  don't leave  also we have her three terrifying  daughters who possess the ability to  turn into a swarm of bugs  and want nothing more than to string  ethan up and eat them alive  man blood also mentions a younger  brother who might possibly be this van  helsing looking [ __ ]  demotrescu and her family are seemingly  the ones behind the kidnapping of  ethan's daughter  all part of a ceremony for one mother  miranda  yes of course i understand the  importance of the ceremony  i won't let you down  so in the game you'll be exploring both  the demotrescue castle  and the surrounding village it's  designed to be one seamless map you can  explore  its overall size is yet to be seen but  there's meant to be a  greater emphasis on exploration than  previous resident evils  gameplay will be building off of the  first person nature of resident evil 7.  this time around  guarding takes even greater importance  to help ethan counter foes  and you have the option to push them  away if you're getting crowded  we've also seen a much greater variety  of enemies which is  excellent news for those that found the  molded in resident evil 7  a little one note we've got these  ghoulish looking boys wearing cloaked  rags and rocking swords and battle axes  in the castle dungeon  meanwhile in the village ethan is  attacked by a group of  beefy hairy werewolf-like men and one  massive  bushy bearded man with a giant hammer  who's given me big  executioner vibes from resident evil 5.  honestly the whole thing kinda feels  like resident evil 4  infused with bloodborne two of my  favorite games ever made  and i am here for it  if it's just looking window shop away  speaking of resident evil 4 village has  a merchant of its own  a lovely fellow known as the duke his  shop lets you buy and sell weapons and  ammo as well as purchase gun upgrades  just like in resident evil 4. also  returning is the tetris style inventory  management system  creating first aid meds is now done from  a new crafting menu  you can also craft ammo just like in  resident evil 3.  the game very much feels like a  collection of the resident evil  franchise's best ideas  fused into one game finally it's worth  mentioning that resident evil village  comes with a free  separate resident evil multiplayer game  called reverse  it's a six-person death match where you  pick your favorite character and  duke it out in iconic resident evil  locations such as the raccoon city  police department  ari vs another game in a long line of  capcom attempting  weird multiplayer focused resident evil  games will this be the one that finally  works out  we'll just have to wait and see  so when can you get your hands on the  game thankfully you only have to wait a  few months as the game releases on may  7th  originally village was only announced  for current gen systems  ie ps5 xbox series x s and pc  but it has now been confirmed for ps4  and xbox one  if that's still too long of a wait and  you're chomping at the bit to try it out  and you  happen to be one of the five people on  the planet that owns a ps5  then you can check out the exclusive  maiden demo it's described as a visual  showcase that is its own  separate experience not part of the full  game if you don't have a ps5  don't worry we capture the whole demo  and you can watch it  right here after this capcom is also  aware that  most people don't have a ps5 so there  will be a separate second demo released  on all platforms  sometime this spring so that's  everything you need to know about  resident evil village  so far it's shaping up to be not only a  fantastic follow-up to resident evil 7  but in many ways a follow up to the  mechanics and themes of  resident evil 4 which is really hard to  not get excited about  hopefully we'll get some hands-on time  with the game before its full release  so make sure to come back to gamespot  for that as well as our full coverage  and review  thanks for watching  you

